      {
        "id": 87510,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-24T19:52:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>danmarshall14 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Obviously not a Playtester, but&nbsp;from what I understand concerning the V5 mechanics, I don't see a reason (and perhaps someone who has played the game and has a reason could prove me wrong!) why a \"mini-expansion\" for Vengeance can't be released at some point down the line.&nbsp; As others have mentioned, there are still a few mini-bosses/smalltime villains present that may not be prime-time enough to appear as a big villain, but could very well be a part of a team.Plus, it'd be pretty safe to assume that &gt;G didn't take all this time to add a completely new way to play the game only to never expand upon it with more options.&nbsp; It'd be cool to see the next mini-expansion offer a&nbsp;smaller villain team or&nbsp;the next \"normal\" expansion contain 2 heroes, 2 environments,&nbsp;2 villains, and a handful of \"minor villains\" that can create more combinations for Vengeance.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nWhat would be really cool is if we could create mini-decks for existing Villains and plug them into the Vengeance format.Plauge Rat for example. Annex a few Plauge cards and some oneshots, house rule up a character card, then plug and play\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Might take a bit to get used to the level of interaction and such, but it should be doable.</p>\n<p>Ambuscade could make a great smaller deck, and La Capitan might take interest in forming a new crew &nbsp;The decks are 20 cards right? &nbsp;Just cutting 5 cards might be tough to balance. &nbsp;Would need to ditch (H) and swarming mechanics. &nbsp;Don't know how targets work (or don't).</p>\n<p>Would any Playtester care to wager a guess at where you would set (H) for conversion, since V5 don't use (H)? &nbsp;I would assume (H)=3 would give the best balance, but I could be wrong there.</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
