      {
        "id": 87511,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-24T20:18:34.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Might take a bit to get used to the level of interaction and such, but it should be doable.Ambuscade could make a great smaller deck, and La Capitan might take interest in forming a new crew &nbsp;The decks are 20 cards right? &nbsp;Just cutting 5 cards might be tough to balance. &nbsp;Would need to ditch (H) and swarming mechanics. &nbsp;Don't know how targets work (or don't).Would any Playtester care to wager a guess at where you would set (H) for conversion, since V5 don't use (H)? &nbsp;I would assume (H)=3 would give the best balance, but I could be wrong there.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It would take some testing to get something right, but just look at what EmoSpite did with Lab Raids. There is no chasm too deep which creativity can not cross.</p>\n<p>Ambuscade. Glad you brought him up. Now, I can't say&nbsp;<em>exactly</em> where I got this notion, but I'v had this little tingly feeling for a little bit now that Ambuscade might do something along the lines of what you are suggesting. There might be crumbs of evidence to support such a feeling, but if they even exist in the first place, I'm sure I won't be the only one to pick up on it eventually.</p>",
