      {
        "id": 87515,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-25T08:41:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ambuscade. Glad you brought him up. Now, I can't say&nbsp;<em>exactly</em> where I got this notion, but I'v had this little tingly feeling for a little bit now that Ambuscade might do something along the lines of what you are suggesting. There might be crumbs of evidence to support such a feeling, but if they even exist in the first place, I'm sure I won't be the only one to pick up on it eventually.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Personally, I kind of feel like it might be Spite, like maybe this connects to why we've seen him in a costume on the back of Freedom Six Wraith.&nbsp; He certainly could stand to have a revised deck.&nbsp; If we want the deck down by 5 cards, well, leaving out the Drugs would certainly work…</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Gislef\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/4af34b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Gislef:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>As a playtester, I'd rather see full villain decks made out of one or more of the V5 villains.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, definitely this.</p>",
